VMware Fusion Installation Guide
This page provides step-by-step instructions for installing VMware Fusion on macOS. I have install VM Fusion for my project.

Prerequisites
Before installing VMware Fusion, verify the following:


Hardware: Any Mac that officially supports macOS 12 Monterey or later (for Fusion 13.x and newer). Apple Silicon and Intel Macs are both supported by the universal installer .

Memory: Minimum 8 GB RAM. 16 GB or more is recommended if you plan to run multiple virtual machines simultaneously .

Disk Space: At least 1.5 GB free for the application, plus at least 5 GB per virtual machine .


Download
Go to the Broadcom Support Portal and sign in (or register for a free account).


Navigate to My Downloads → Free Software Downloads.

Search for VMware Fusion and select the latest version (e.g., Fusion 26.Hx).

Read and accept the Terms and Conditions. If the download icon remains disabled, refresh the page or try a different browser without network restrictions .

Download the .dmg file. The same installer works for both Intel and Apple Silicon Macs .

Licensing Note: VMware Fusion is free for personal, educational, and commercial use. No license key is required — during installation, select "Use for Personal Use" or leave the license field blank .

Installation Steps
Open the DMG: Double-click the downloaded VMware-Fusion-*.dmg file to mount it.

Launch the Installer: In the Finder window that appears, double-click the VMware Fusion icon (or drag it to the Applications folder). Installing Fusion 13 will automatically remove any older version of Fusion .

Confirm the Open Warning: If macOS displays "application downloaded from the internet," click Open.

Authenticate: Enter your macOS administrator password when prompted. This is required for the one-time setup of network and system components .

Accept the License Agreement: Review and click Agree to proceed.

Complete Setup: Enter the administrator password again if prompted. The initialization will finish, and VMware Fusion will be installed in /Applications.

Verify Installation
Launch VMware Fusion from Applications or Spotlight. You should see the Virtual Machine Library window or the Installation Assistant. If the application opens without errors, the installation is complete.
